batdetect binary distribution

The batdetect source code is licensed under the MIT License (LICENSE). This binary also
contains, statically linked, the components below, each under its own license. Their
license texts are in licenses/.

Source of this binary: the tag v<version> printed by `batdetect --version`, at
https://github.com/zaratan/chiro-dvr/tags. The GitHub release of that tag holds this
archive, the source code of batdetect, and the sources of FFmpeg and openh264 it was
built from.

FFmpeg 7.1.1, GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1 or later
(licenses/FFmpeg-LGPL-2.1.txt)
  Copyright (c) 2000-2025 the FFmpeg developers, https://ffmpeg.org
  Built without --enable-gpl and without --enable-nonfree, so no GPL part of FFmpeg is
  included. Enabled components: libavcodec (h264 and hevc decoders and parsers, the
  libopenh264 encoder, and on macOS VideoToolbox decoding and the h264_videotoolbox
  encoder), libavformat (mov demuxer, mp4 muxer, file protocol), libswscale and libavutil.
  Source: ffmpeg-7.1.1.tar.xz, attached to the release.
  To relink batdetect with a modified FFmpeg: in the source of the tag, point FFMPEG_URL
  (a file:// URL works) and FFMPEG_SHA256 of packaging/ffmpeg-versions to the modified
  archive, run packaging/ffmpeg-unix.sh (or packaging/ffmpeg-windows.sh), then
  `cargo build --release -p batdetect` from a clean target directory.

